1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:04,935
Imagine driving a car where everything you see happened three seconds ago,

2
00:00:04,975 --> 00:00:07,172
and the car obeys three seconds late.

3
00:00:07,212 --> 00:00:09,022
That is every day on Mars.

4
00:00:09,062 --> 00:00:10,925
So who do you trust to drive?

5
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:13,055
We built that day.

6
00:00:13,095 --> 00:00:16,768
One rover, one day of sunlight, rocks to collect, and one rule:

7
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,908
be home before the battery dies.

8
00:00:20,758 --> 00:00:24,243
Then we handed the keys to nine AI models from three labs,

9
00:00:24,283 --> 00:00:26,493
from the fastest to the most powerful.

10
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:28,508
Surely one of them makes it home?

11
00:00:29,875 --> 00:00:31,285
Mars doesn't play fair.

12
00:00:31,325 --> 00:00:34,523
A fast one reaches for a rock and misses, by 3 centimetres.

13
00:00:34,563 --> 00:00:35,472
No points.

14
00:00:35,512 --> 00:00:37,400
9 tries, 1 rock.

15
00:00:38,725 --> 00:00:41,035
A bigger one drives onto a slope too steep.

16
00:00:41,075 --> 00:00:43,398
The rover freezes and forgets its orders.

17
00:00:43,438 --> 00:00:44,800
30 times.

18
00:00:46,325 --> 00:00:50,385
And a flagship: 13 metres from home, 21 samples on board.

19
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:51,775
It will not make it.

20
00:00:53,575 --> 00:00:54,335
Nothing broke.

21
00:00:54,375 --> 00:00:55,675
So what went wrong?

22
00:00:57,225 --> 00:00:57,785
The sun.

23
00:00:57,825 --> 00:00:59,110
It's the only fuel.

24
00:00:59,150 --> 00:01:02,100
This rover drove until its battery was flat.

25
00:01:04,908 --> 00:01:08,181
Our driver saw its battery fall, stopped, and waited for light.

26
00:01:08,221 --> 00:01:09,908
So how did all nine do?

27
00:01:11,258 --> 00:01:13,918
On three maps in a row, none beat our driver.

28
00:01:13,958 --> 00:01:15,493
The best run came within a hair;

29
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:18,443
the best average brought home 37%.

30
00:01:18,483 --> 00:01:21,380
Ours: 48, and it never lost a rover.

31
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:22,658
So what is it?

32
00:01:24,716 --> 00:01:25,626
Not an AI.

33
00:01:25,666 --> 00:01:29,439
A planner: plain code that works out the whole day before the wheels turn.

34
00:01:29,479 --> 00:01:30,276
Lucky maps?

35
00:01:30,316 --> 00:01:31,641
We wondered too.

36
00:01:33,516 --> 00:01:38,351
So we replayed every model's best program on 300 fresh worlds, on Modal.

37
00:01:38,391 --> 00:01:41,151
The planner won 95 times in 100.

38
00:01:41,191 --> 00:01:43,166
Can a machine learn it instead?

39
00:01:44,491 --> 00:01:46,151
We trained one from scratch.

40
00:01:46,191 --> 00:01:48,576
On average it out-scored 8 of the 9 models,

41
00:01:48,616 --> 00:01:50,541
and still lost to the planner.

42
00:01:52,841 --> 00:01:54,151
AI can write the code.

43
00:01:54,191 --> 00:01:55,626
It can't yet plan the day.

44
00:01:55,666 --> 00:01:57,416
Can your agent make it home?

